      "side": 1,
      "message": "We reviewed what happens on the Trusty side if we run out of retries:\n* For the creation message, if Trusty gets enough cycles with `FFA_RUN` then it will successfully create the VM and put it in the `FRESH` state (but not available). TZ shouldn\u0027t get stuck here, worst case that happens is that VM leaks.\n* Destruction message: if Trusty never returns success here, then the VM stays in one of the `NOTIFYING` states and never reaches `READY_TO_FREE`, which means it leaks.\n\nThe TEE should otherwise continue functioning normally, since the actual work done for the VM messages is on a separate thread that can sleep independently.",
      "revId": "da6c66e034af103e466967404ac3b6496f2a212c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
